From 0a4391ef3479abef1c4bf0d726bac7f8e3696b36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: consnop <consnop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:42:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Show only the patched build in the firmware picker on
 patched boards

The "Choose a PebbleOS build" picker still listed Core's releases through
api.github.com on obelix_pvt, so behind a shared IP it stopped at "rate
limited" and could not install the patched build the update check had
just offered. On boards in PATCHED_REVISIONS it now offers exactly what
the update check does: the feed's build, preselected, or nothing newer,
or the check's failure. It also can no longer list a stock build that
would drop the patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J4cyE5MpWNo2QG1iuNRXKQ
